body:
Introducing git_config_level_t is a nice idea for type safety, however, this limits flexibility (and breaks some third-party code).
E.g. TortoiseGit uses an extra level to maintain an extra config-file on top of the normal ones (compare https://github.com/TortoiseGit/TortoiseGit/commit/4d603ef8eec41c59077eff6046a79a32707e9404, https://github.com/TortoiseGit/TortoiseGit/blob/4d603ef8eec41c59077eff6046a79a32707e9404/src/TortoiseProc/ProjectProperties.cpp#L114). Now, this isn't possible any more w/o patching libgit2.
@vmg
